#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088090 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9fbd335c-28cc-5f02-b773-f685e8b15417" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Image of a Vector Sum Under a Map Using Vector Addition and Scalar Multiplication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab20db60-9386-5af8-9288-d296521ae534" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}162 \\\\ -108 \\\\ 90\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085472} {:answer/id #uuid "b4709435-5443-5105-9e32-277431b519d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}108 \\\\ -72 \\\\ 60\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085473} {:answer/id #uuid "ca0d49d0-cd63-541f-a015-1ff9cf20f465" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}18 \\\\ -12 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085474} {:answer/id #uuid "095ca38e-89fd-55b2-af01-e498752002ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085475} {:answer/id #uuid "64d34854-7d43-5bdc-bc15-6fe9f5d0f73e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}27 \\\\ -18 \\\\ 15\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085476}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab20db60-9386-5af8-9288-d296521ae534" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}162 \\\\ -108 \\\\ 90\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085472} :answer-field/id #uuid "ad8c4863-b8f6-5a20-8167-8a3bc0e10f48" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085471}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "edb52688-79ea-5f71-b873-96bf082190d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-37873" :question/problem "Consider a linear transformation $\\,T\\,.$ If $\\,{v}_{1}+{v}_{2}=0\\,$ and $\\,T({v}_{1})=[\\begin{aligned}54 \\\\ -36 \\\\ 30\\end{aligned}]\\,$, find $\\,T(21{v}_{1}+18{v}_{2}).$" :question/worked-solution "First, since ${v}_{1}+{v}_{2}=0,$ we have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}21{v}_{1}+18{v}_{2} & =18{v}_{1}+3{v}_{1}+18{v}_{2} \\\\  & =18({v}_{1}+{v}_{2})+3{v}_{1} \\\\  & =18(0)+3{v}_{1} \\\\  & =3{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nT(21{v}_{1}+18{v}_{2})=T(3{v}_{1}).\n$$\n\nNow, since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that $T(kv)=kT(v).$ So \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(3{v}_{1}) & =3T({v}_{1}) \\\\  & =3[\\begin{aligned}54 \\\\ -36 \\\\ 30\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}162 \\\\ -108 \\\\ 90\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn conclusion, $T(21{v}_{1}+18{v}_{2})=[\\begin{aligned}162 \\\\ -108 \\\\ 90\\end{aligned}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088091 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "381f7ffe-ae4b-5e45-9fa9-e2a6bd8348b3" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Image of a Vector Under a Map Using Vector Addition and Scalar Multiplication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "912948ff-f9a1-5e65-a839-3224e5593cec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 18\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085478} {:answer/id #uuid "bdf3f517-8e44-53c7-9026-1c3f07d5da55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085479} {:answer/id #uuid "155a6bec-24b9-56d4-92fd-68891f45f8c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085480} {:answer/id #uuid "1c7692bf-89ca-5145-95ef-7648348d18f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 15\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085481} {:answer/id #uuid "4dce2a1b-0076-5d92-8dc9-748f3b846712" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085482}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4dce2a1b-0076-5d92-8dc9-748f3b846712" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085482} :answer-field/id #uuid "f73514b8-149c-51c3-b988-f1916e58cf5b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085477}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "00d97500-f2d6-5911-b246-c9aee29ac1dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-37898" :question/problem "Consider a linear transformation $\\,T\\,.$ If $\\,T({v}_{1}+3{v}_{2})=[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,T({v}_{1})=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}]$, then find $\\,T({v}_{2}).$" :question/worked-solution "Since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v+kw)=T(v)+T(kw)=T(v)+kT(w)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor any vectors $v$ and $w.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T({v}_{1}+3{v}_{2}) & =T({v}_{1})+3T({v}_{2}) \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}]+3T({v}_{2}) \\\\ 3T({v}_{2}) & =[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}] \\\\ 3T({v}_{2}) & =[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({v}_{2}) & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({v}_{2}) & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262654 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "381f7ffe-ae4b-5e45-9fa9-e2a6bd8348b3" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Image of a Vector Under a Map Using Vector Addition and Scalar Multiplication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "471db198-499e-53ab-bde4-7f405b035dbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262656} {:answer/id #uuid "d2bd33c6-19d7-5a88-a88c-c8f48e942d66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262657} {:answer/id #uuid "ebdff365-0d82-5773-b245-ec0f4c32b657" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262658} {:answer/id #uuid "03eaa1f8-6908-539e-b1a9-5c16d08c6632" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262659} {:answer/id #uuid "46d6be46-15b2-52b7-82ea-ba26b3040f35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262660}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "03eaa1f8-6908-539e-b1a9-5c16d08c6632" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262659} :answer-field/id #uuid "e228ddcc-0ebd-586f-b279-9dad1b31844d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262655}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "57cbc13b-b004-59d3-9b49-913460c9f9b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-74775" :question/problem "Consider a linear transformation $\\,T\\,.$ If $\\,T(3{v}_{1}+7{v}_{2})=[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,T({v}_{2})=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$, then find $\\,T({v}_{1}).$" :question/worked-solution "Since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(kv+hw)=T(kv)+T(hw)=kT(v)+hT(w)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor any vectors $v$ and $w.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(3{v}_{1}+7{v}_{2}) & =3T({v}_{1})+7T({v}_{2}) \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] & =3T({v}_{1})+7[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ 3T({v}_{1}) & =[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]-7[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ 3T({v}_{1}) & =[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ 3T({v}_{1}) & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({v}_{1}) & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({v}_{1}) & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354876 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9fbd335c-28cc-5f02-b773-f685e8b15417" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Image of a Vector Sum Under a Map Using Vector Addition and Scalar Multiplication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4715a94f-0da4-5045-820c-ca8b533f5932" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}64 \\\\ -32 \\\\ -72\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354878} {:answer/id #uuid "9cbf06d8-b7ae-5735-85df-36c0a77670b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}40 \\\\ -20 \\\\ -45\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354879} {:answer/id #uuid "46d9cda0-53aa-595e-940b-2ee701c33df4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-64 \\\\ 32 \\\\ 72\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354880} {:answer/id #uuid "8e298117-c97c-5ee4-830a-04ccc3393618" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-40 \\\\ 20 \\\\ 45\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354881} {:answer/id #uuid "873dab30-b0b1-5c58-a91a-b667ba08b91b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354882}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9cbf06d8-b7ae-5735-85df-36c0a77670b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}40 \\\\ -20 \\\\ -45\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354879} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ac0d906-d18d-5aeb-8c3f-147516677eea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354877}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "842ea3a5-ec4a-5793-8b5a-6977864aa68e" :question/math-academy-id "q-74780" :question/problem "Consider a linear transformation $\\,T\\,.$ If $\\,{v}_{1}+{v}_{2}=0\\,$ and $\\,T({v}_{2})=[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]\\,$, find $\\,T(13{v}_{1}+8{v}_{2}).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}13{v}_{1}+8{v}_{2} & =13{v}_{1}+13{v}_{2}-5{v}_{2} \\\\  & =13({v}_{1}+{v}_{2})-5{v}_{2} \\\\  & =13(0)-5{v}_{2} \\\\  & =-5{v}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nT(13{v}_{1}+8{v}_{2})=T(-5{v}_{2}).\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that $T(kv)=kT(v).$ So \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(-5{v}_{2}) & =-5T({v}_{2}) \\\\  & =-5[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}40 \\\\ -20 \\\\ -45\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn conclusion, $T(13{v}_{1}+8{v}_{2})=[\\begin{aligned}40 \\\\ -20 \\\\ -45\\end{aligned}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088361 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8c04b23-e341-57e9-a072-985e4b536e5a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Linear Transformations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "865035a9-dfe6-51bf-a5dc-624240267541" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087097} {:answer/id #uuid "981d3229-34da-5547-9622-76e7a57b9b97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087098} {:answer/id #uuid "ff08f834-c93c-58b6-a6eb-be4ab302b1ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087099} {:answer/id #uuid "5826ab39-99cb-5f0d-a91a-c8e47d4e7431" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087100} {:answer/id #uuid "58fc334c-401e-58ca-8084-7bbee1c81411" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087101}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "865035a9-dfe6-51bf-a5dc-624240267541" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087097} :answer-field/id #uuid "212166f2-0485-5ec6-aaa6-538998150651" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087096}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a9a96319-3bb3-5dd4-a3ac-27f5effab07d" :question/math-academy-id "q-8331" :question/problem "Let \n$T:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}y \\\\ x\\end{aligned}].$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $T(kv)=kT(v)$ for any real $2\\times 1$ column vector $v$ and real scalar $k$\n- $T({v}_{1}+{v}_{2})=T({v}_{1})+T({v}_{2})$ for any real $2\\times 1$ column vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$\n- $T$ is a linear transformation" :question/worked-solution "A linear transformation $T$ satisfies two properties:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & T[\\begin{aligned}kx \\\\ ky\\end{aligned}]=kT[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}], \\\\  & T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Checking the first condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T[\\begin{aligned}kx \\\\ ky\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}ky \\\\ kx\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =k[\\begin{aligned}y \\\\ x\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =kT[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}].\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Checking the second condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}+{y}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{T}$ is a linear transformation.\n\nAs a result, all three statements are true."}]}
